Last Saturday, I had breakfast at Balthazar in NYC and thought:  
"How hard could it be to run a classic French bistro?"  
So I built a 3D game.  

Introducing Bistro School (bistroschool. app).  
You own a one-Michelin-star French bistro, and your goal is to reach three stars without having a nervous breakdown.  

To win, you have to channel Will Guidara’s "Unreasonable Hospitality" and Danny Meyer’s "What Could Possibly Go Right?" (mostly while everything goes wrong).  

Naturally, simulating a 19th-century dining room required a completely normal, restrained budget for tech stack (wink wink):
